Patch-Source: https://git.musl-libc.org/cgit/musl/commit/?id=5e03c03fcde3534b37a0b995a438cd176d6882d3
Subject: clone: align the given stack pointer on riscv32

Backport of the riscv32 half of upstream musl commit 5e03c03f (2025-02-22),
released after 1.2.5. pthread_create only rounds the child stack down to
sizeof(uintptr_t) -- 4 on ILP32 -- and then subtracts the 20-byte start_args,
which inverts the mod-8 residue. __clone never repairs it, so every non-main
thread runs at sp % 8 == 4 for its whole life.

The RISC-V ILP32 psABI spills 64-bit variadic arguments to an 8-aligned slot in
a save area the callee builds from its incoming sp, so a misaligned frame makes
every 64-bit va_arg in a worker thread read garbage. Observed as CPython's
test_threading deadlocking on Condition/RLock, whose _release_save returns the
owner ident through Py_BuildValue("kK", ...).

--- a/src/thread/riscv32/clone.s
+++ b/src/thread/riscv32/clone.s
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 .type  __clone, %function
 __clone:
 	# Save func and arg to stack
+	andi a1, a1, -16
 	addi a1, a1, -16
 	sw a0, 0(a1)
 	sw a3, 4(a1)
